                <head>Enclosure in Above</head>
                <p rendition="#flush"><hi rendition="#italic">Article concerning freedom of transit
                        for telegraphic correspondence and telephonic communications to be inserted
                        in the Treaty of Peace with Austria</hi></p>
                <p>Notwithstanding any contrary stipulation in existing Treaties Austria undertakes
                    to grant freedom of transit for telegraphic correspondence and telephonic
                    communications coming from or going to any one of the Allied and Associated
                    Powers whether neighbours or not over such lines as may be most suitable for
                    international transit and in accordance with the tariffs in force. This
                    correspondence and these communications shall be subjected to no unnecessary
                    delay or restriction; they shall enjoy in Austria national treatment in regard
                    to every kind of facility and especially in regard to rapidity of transmission.
                    No payment, facility or restriction shall depend directly or indirectly on the
                    nationality of the transmitter or the addressee.</p>
            </div>
